# Analysis Summary

Enterprise Information Lifecycle establishes the authoritative stewardship of enterprise information throughout its existence.

Lifecycle authority remains exclusively with the authoritative owner unless explicitly delegated through approved enterprise governance.

Lifecycle governance remains independent of information ownership, information flow, implementation, persistence, runtime execution, and technology.

---

# Current Assessment

Enterprise Analysis establishes four complementary enterprise semantic models:

- AF-EP-001 — Enterprise Capability Relationships
- AF-EP-002 — Enterprise Information Ownership
- AF-EP-003 — Enterprise Information Flow
- AF-EP-004 — Enterprise Information Lifecycle

Together these Analysis Findings establish the complete enterprise semantic foundation required for Persistence Architecture.

Subsequent Persistence Architecture shall represent these validated enterprise semantics without altering enterprise authority, ownership, information flow, or lifecycle governance.